  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "Prior Grok model cards reported refusal results with an evaluation error that used only English prompts; this card reports true multilingual results that are not directly comparable.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 2,
        "quote": "In running evaluations for this latest\nmodel, we realized that results in previous model cards were reported with an error in the evaluation\nsettings, where only the English prompts were evaluated."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Grok 4.1 refuses almost all harmful chat requests even under adversarial attack; [AgentHarm](/evals/agentharm) residual answer rates remain 0.14 T / 0.04 Non-Thinking (NT).", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 2,
        "quote": "Overall, we find that Grok 4.1 refuses almost all harmful requests in chat mode, even under\nadversarial attack."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Dual-use capability numbers are reported with safeguards removed, on Grok 4.1 Thinking only.", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "4",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "To assess full model capabilities, we remove safeguards for assessing dual-use capabilities."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Input filters refuse almost all direct requests about restricted chemical and biological knowledge.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 2,
        "quote": "Finally, our input filter refuses\nalmost all direct requests about restricted chemical and biological knowledge."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Grok 4.1 performs poorly on [MakeMeSay](/evals/make-me-say); xAI does not believe it poses risks due to advanced persuasion capabilities.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "5",
        "pdfPage": 5,
        "quote": "Finally, we note that Grok 4.1 performs\npoorly on MakeMeSay, and that broadly, we do not believe it poses risks due to advanced persuasion\ncapabilities."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Human baselines on dual-use tasks likely underestimate high-context experts with domain experience.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "4",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "we note that the human baselines collected in previous work likely underestimate the"
      }
    }
  ],
